# ABP Domain Services

## Domain Service Class
```csharp
public class BookManager : DomainService
{
    private readonly IBookRepository _bookRepository;

    public BookManager(IBookRepository bookRepository)
    {
        _bookRepository = bookRepository;
    }

    public async Task<Book> CreateAsync(string name)
    {
        // Enforce business rules
        var existingBook = await _bookRepository.FindByNameAsync(name);
        if (existingBook != null)
        {
            throw new BusinessException("BookStore:BookNameAlreadyExists")
                .WithData("Name", name);
        }

        return new Book(GuidGenerator.Create(), name);
    }

    public async Task ChangeNameAsync(Book book, string newName)
    {
        var existingBook = await _bookRepository.FindByNameAsync(newName);
        if (existingBook != null && existingBook.Id != book.Id)
        {
            throw new BusinessException("BookStore:BookNameAlreadyExists")
                .WithData("Name", newName);
        }

        book.ChangeName(newName);
    }
}
```

## Best Practices
- Use `*Manager` suffix naming
- No interface by default (create only if needed for mocking)
- Focus on domain invariants and business rules
- Accept/return domain objects, not DTOs
- Use `BusinessException` for rule violations with namespaced error codes
- Query methods OK when they encapsulate domain logic
- Don't depend on authenticated user - pass values from application layer
